{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_ICVoPT289w64mKRvrJEU82CD","content":"1\t# Literature reading reference · plan r3\n2\t\n3\t**Status: r3, 2026-11-23. Revised after the first panel round; not yet\n4\tapproved.** r2 was the full plan `start-milestone` wrote from outline r1\n5\t(2026-11-22, merged in PR 229). The owner delegated `auto=true` for this\n6\tmilestone on 2026-11-23 and selected the full GND panel for plan and close\n7\treview (D6). The first round read r2\n8\t([r2 panel](../../../reviews/literature-reading-reference-r2-panel/README.md));\n9\tr3 applies its seven fixes, listed in §11. Approval is recorded only in a\n10\tplan-gate record, which does not exist yet.\n11\t\n12\tThis plan covers one open issue,\n13\t[#226](https://github.com/vasiloglou/gnd-public/issues/226): a host reading\n14\tscientific papers with GND's literature stages measured about 30 % recall for\n15\tevery model it tried and has no reference point to tell its own loss from the\n16\tmethod's.\n17\t\n18\t**Provenance.** Phase IDs LR1–LR3 and decisions D1–D5 are the outline's. r2\n19\tadds criteria IDs, obligations H1–H22 and decisions D6–D9. The outline left\n20\ttwo rows \"not read\". Both are read now, and both change the plan `(r2)`:\n21\t\n22\t- **LR1.** `gnd verify --format json` already lists every failing constraint\n23\t  with its rows (H2). What is missing is a page that says so, the rows in the\n24\t  text output, and the constraint's declared id (H3, H4).\n25\t- **LR2.** The reading example has no quote and refuses none (H8). The 44\n26\t  claims #226 lost to \"quote outside the shown section\" were dropped by the\n27\t  reporter's own host. GND's one binding of a quote to text is the anchor\n28\t  check, against the whole document a sidecar names (H10).\n29\t\n30\tr3 adds H23–H25 and re-ran H2–H4 and H22 at `11a7ebf7` `(r3)`. Code\n31\tcitations were read at `548b9a1d` (`main`, 2026-11-23). `main` moved to\n32\t`78934ee3` the same day (PR 234, PR 236, PR 237) while this plan