ge (D7).\n68\t- **R0.2 A reference figure is a measurement of one run.** It names the\n69\t  producer, the settings and the labelled set. It is not a claim about other\n70\t  corpora or models, and the page says so beside every figure.\n71\t- **R0.3 No fidelity rate in the `verify` payload.** `gnd verify` keeps\n72\t  saying that checker acceptance is not proof of faithfulness\n73\t  (`extraction-contract.md:152`); the reference figures live in the\n74\t  example's own record.\n75\t- **R0.4 Fixture bytes stay.** The packaged reading run, its pinned producer\n76\t  table and its recorded outputs are byte-identical after LR1 and LR2. LR3\n77\t  adds a second fixture beside them and changes none.\n78\t- **R0.5 The gate calls no model.** A live run happens once, under the\n79\t  owner's explicit selection of a producer and a budget (D3). Every gate\n80\t  replays recorded responses.\n81\t- **R0.6 One home per rule.** How to read a failed verification has one\n82\t  home (D8); the quote rule lives in `docs/reference/anchors.md`; the\n83\t  literature pages cite both.\n84\t\n85\tThe project's six standing rules\n86\t(`.codex/skills/process-phase/references/project.md`) and the rule \"General\n87\tsolutions, not pattern-matched ones\" (`AGENTS.md`) bind every phase; each\n88\tspec discharges them by name.\n89\t\n90\t## 1. Scope, sources and authority\n91\t\n92\tHarvested obligations. \"Observed\" means read or run by the author at\n93\t`548b9a1d` on 2026-11-23; \"agent\" means read by the harvest agent;\n94\t\"inherited\" means claimed by a source and not re-measured.\n95\t\n96\t| # | Source | Obligation | Kind | Phase |\n97\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n98\t| H1 | #226 request 3 | \"A way to see why `verify` reports `alethic-failure` per source: which constraint, on which rows.\" The reporter saw it on all 20 sources (3,729 rows, 280 of them unanchored) | inherited | LR1 |\n99\t| H2 | probe `(r3)`: run `python -m gnd.examples.literature.reading run --out RUN`, copy `reading_fix